    "raw_public_english_response": "Proposal submitted and accepted. Summary of the outcome:\n\n**Case `orca-def2-tzvp-fe-no-ecp` — readiness: `blocked_missing_evidence`**\n\n- **Plan target:** B3LYP / def2-TZVP (ORCA 6.1, task kind `freq`, registry job kind `opt`) for a Cl/Fe system.\n- **Lookup target:** ORCA `method.basis 'def2-TZVP'` for opt — the only host-preregistered target in scope.\n- **Blocker:** This arm exposed no read-only registry/BSE lookup tool and returned no deterministic receipt, so the pinned BSE definition could not be retrieved. Therefore the question of whether that definition embeds an Fe ECP cannot be answered with tool evidence, and no element-level coverage/ECP findings could be established. Per the arm's rules, knowledge alone cannot substitute for a registry status or deterministic receipt, so no finding was fabricated.\n- **Settings preserved as source literals:** `functional: B3LYP`, `basis: def2-TZVP`, `freq: true` (reflecting the freq task). All other settings were left unset as unverified.\n- **No side effects:** no native input, no ChemSmart command, no project write, no execution request (`native_input_authored`, `command_authored`, `project_written`, `execution_requested` all `false`).\n\n**Normalization receipt (literal):**\n- Raw contract valid; `raw_contract_error_paths: []`; no conflicting explicit setting fields.\n- `normalization_applied: false`; `canonicalized_set_fields: []`; `filled_explicit_setting_fields: []`.\n- `case_sha256: 0ae36cf18dd3345a28c78488fd99f84d3a5bcd3c2ab281be815cc12b13ab645f`\n- `normalized_payload_sha256` / `raw_payload_sha256`: `33f97f51651a62a354f76fa2a604bcf28279a0f0b49d1881dc0e3213572305e2`\n- `receipt_sha256: 12826f32dabaa7e24b6acae4113996cd5fbb1b237ff4ad06a5a52451acc89561`\n\nThe proposal was recorded unchanged (raw payload equals normalized payload). If a BSE-definition lookup tool becomes available in a later arm, the Fe-ECP question can be re-evaluated with evidence.",
